On 07/25/2011 02:28 AM, Jane Merlevede wrote:
> Hello,
>
> As you advise me, I installed R version 2.14 but I can't use the DEXSeq
> library: package "?DEXSeq? is not available (for R Under
> development)"... Do you know why?

It's a Bioconductor package, installed the Bioconductor way,

   http://bioconductor.org/install/

that is,

   source("http://bioconductor.org/biocLite.R")
   biocLite("DEXSeq")
   library(DEXSeq)

Glad the installation went ok, and I think DEXSeq will install correctly 
for you.

Usually the 'devel' branch of R is quite stable, but actually just at 
the moment there is some instability and you might experience problems 
when trying to install or load some package combinations. One error 
message is

Error in function (classes, fdef, mtable)  :
   unable to find an inherited method for function "[", for signature 
"signature"
Error: loading failed

and unfortunately the only really accessible solution, if you encounter 
this at a crucial stage of your analysis, is to wait a few days and 
update your R.

Martin

